<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Claymore</h1>
<p>Average Length: Approx. up to 6'
Type of Weapon: Distanced Hand-to-hand.
</p><p>The claymore (from the Scottish Gaelic for “great sword”): While the name "claymore" came to refer to the Scottish basket-hilted sword, the broadsword, by the end of the 17th century, the true claymore was a Scottish two-handed weapon of the 15th and 16th centuries.
</p><p>The two-handed claymore was a huge weapon designed to crush through armored and unarmored opponents alike. Often as long as six feet from the tip to pommel (the hilt-end of the weapon), special arrangements were given to those warriors wielding claymores in combat because of the space needed to swing them. The claymore is characterized by a long, double edged blade and downward slanting quillons.
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="In_Valhalla">In Valhalla</span></h2>
<p>In Valhalla the claymore is a weapon skill of its own, one of the swords (see <a cmd='#'>Help Weapons</a>): two-handed, it slashes, it leans on strength, with some dexterity, and it is slow, as two-handed weapons are. It is taught by the barbarians from guild level 25.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
